/pull/121531.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121531.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"- Closes #121518\r\n\r\n~~Also added a `world_3d_changed` signal to `Viewport` because I couldn't find another clean way of updating whenever the viewport world changed. Not sure if this is best apporach, lmk. Don't like adding an API like that for no reason.~~\r\n\r\nSwitched the signal approach with a static function pointer on `Viewport` that points to `_viewport_world_3d_changed` on `Node3DEditor`.\r\n\r\nThis implementation was my idea, but AI helped a bit with some code. I have reviewed every line and tested with the test project provided here/in the issue, and my personal project that had issues with this. Seems to work fine.\r\n\r\nAlso - setting `use_world_3d` to false seems to trigger this error:\r\n`ERROR: servers\\rendering\\renderer_scene_cull.cpp:497 - Parameter \"scenario\" is null.`\r\nThis was already the case before my PR so I did not touch it.\r\n\r\nExample video:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/52ab9bf5-a7c2-4fc4-a152-c3e5fe939746\r\n\r\nExample project:\r\n[viewport_world_test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30150780/viewport_world_test.zip)\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121531/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121531/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}